  "proof_file_sha256": "be5d7125a72d5bb5cf84cec9c309997cbb02d2f06b1e866e421a7578fa1e935f",
  "review_scope": "Read all seven blocks and compared the literal finite-and-growth conclusion, actual SecM scalar action, power-coordinate maps and PolAV/isAb records. Verified Milne's primary Proposition 9.1 and Theorem 13.3(b),(c). The final boundary explicitly preserves SHV17 eventual all-cover Serre and SHV21 homogeneous generation, distinguishing the later every-positive-power descent input. No whole selected obligation is closed.",
  "claims_reviewed": [
    {
      "id": "SGV1",
      "block_sha256": "62b4b0fd65d717509f5041fae43b4cfdc56691509aa853994ff10b8c81444619",
      "result": "PASS",
      "mathematical_review": "The specific projection from the identity-base categorical product has an explicit inverse by its universal property. Smooth proper geometrically connected fibers with identity are regular and geometrically integral; the original smoothDim field gives exactly g. This verifies Milne's abelian-variety hypotheses on the actual product."
    },
    {
      "id": "SGV2",
      "block_sha256": "ab25d65b3e611adb2b7223ea9d671d5f0c6074e62b6345be8ca3e4e558b51d72",
      "result": "PASS",
      "mathematical_review": "The singleton power charts have precisely the pulled transition units to exponent j. The source SecM equations and toSec/ofSec keep coordinate tuples unchanged. The original first-projection scalar action agrees with the canonical K-to-global-functions isomorphism, for positive and negative powers."
    },
    {
      "id": "SGV3",
      "block_sha256": "ac7236fbe11bc85a56334d1a5f7c2dd85dc68be867ab6bdd45a529d4c068f63f",
      "result": "PASS",
      "mathematical_review": "PBC26 supplies one N before t on the actual Cartesian model. The original ratio-surjectivity data give a closed immersion chart by chart. A section nonzero at the identity stays nonzero in every positive tensor power, and Veronese preserves ampleness in all characteristics. The power-coordinate maps identify V_(Nt) literally."
    },
    {
      "id": "SGV4",
      "block_sha256": "48cef665a4b37e82c4d35c97176959b3b83490a7e955fcfb55c9ffb9fe8907e8",
      "result": "PASS",
      "mathematical_review": "Milne Proposition 9.1 applies because each positive power is ample with a nonzero section; Theorem 13.3(c) then forces its unique nonzero cohomology degree to be zero. No identification with source KTriv or prime-to-characteristic condition is needed."
    },
    {
      "id": "SGV5",
      "block_sha256": "f788fd38d6ffdc5f4608cd62332c5cc9f71be6df9bc0ade87e5231d1fb883e23",
      "result": "PASS",
      "mathematical_review": "The original nonzero section of a line bundle on the integral scheme defines an effective Cartier divisor. Applying the stated abelian Riemann–Roch formula and multilinearity gives exact t^g scaling. The factorial is used in rational intersection numbers, not inverted inside K."
    },
    {
      "id": "SGV6",
      "block_sha256": "06d76a9d73172fe05e7124e94f62a5e5880e90b034bf2e34270a942c187cecc2",
      "result": "PASS",
      "mathematical_review": "For g=0 the actual geometrically integral finite-type scheme has one point and is Spec of a finite algebraic field extension; algebraic closedness identifies it with K. Every invertible sheaf has one-dimensional sections, giving the same formula."
    },
    {
      "id": "SGV7",
      "block_sha256": "7f2f25cfb4fef2402b746e2dfbab9760567b413ddb74026cfb69e7ecfb688549",
      "result": "PASS",
      "mathematical_review": "PBC27 gives all integer-power finiteness. The fixed N and d=h0(H)>=1 yield exact dimension d*t^g and the literal two-sided contract with c=1,C=d. Original choice order, scalar field, every characteristic and g=0 are retained. Rank one and torsion decomposition remain separate."
    }
  ],
